{#
  ============================================================================
  MARKETPLACE HEADER  -  noon-style two-row layout
  ============================================================================
  This is the file that proves the Twig-vs-React point. In a React Twilight
  theme the header belongs to the engine and can only be injected around
  (header:start / header:end append only - I read HookSlot's source). Here the
  theme owns every tag, so the header can actually be restructured.

  WHAT CHANGED FROM THE STOCK HEADER
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Stock Salla renders a utility top-navbar, then a white main-nav holding
  logo + menu + cart. Measured on the live store that came to 134px, with the
  search stranded in the top row away from everything else.

  noon uses two rows and puts search at the centre of the first:
    row 1 (accent) - logo | location | SEARCH (widest thing) | user | cart
    row 2 (white)  - category menu, one fixed-height scrolling line

  Search is the widest element on purpose. On a marketplace search IS the
  primary navigation, not a utility tucked into a corner.

  EVERY SALLA COMPONENT FROM THE STOCK HEADER IS KEPT
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  salla-search, salla-cart-summary, salla-user-menu, salla-localization-modal,
  salla-bullet-delivery-tag, salla-contacts, custom-main-menu and the scopes
  button are all still here - only their arrangement changed. Dropping any of
  them silently removes real storefront features (language switch, branch
  picker, cart drawer), which is why this is a re-layout and not a rewrite
  from a blank file.

  Heights come from --mp-header-top / --mp-header-nav in _mp-tokens.scss so
  sticky offsets below cannot drift out of sync with the header - which is how
  the menu ended up pinned to the bottom of the bar on the live store.

  | Variable         | Type    | Description                     |
  |------------------|---------|---------------------------------|
  | cart             | object  |                                 |
  | cart.items_count | int     |                                 |
  | cart.total       | string  | Formatted total ex: "١٠٠ ر.س"   |
#}
{% set important_links = theme.settings.get('important_links') %}

<header data-testid="store-header" class="store-header mp-header">

  {# Delivery tag keeps its own full-width row on mobile, as before. #}
  <div class="lg:hidden">
    <salla-bullet-delivery-tag></salla-bullet-delivery-tag>
  </div>

  {# ==========================================================================
     ROW 1 - the accent bar
     ========================================================================== #}
  <div class="mp-header__bar">
    <div class="container mp-header__inner">

      {# ---- Mobile menu toggle -------------------------------------------
         First in DOM order so it is the first thing a keyboard or screen
         reader meets on small screens, where it is the primary control. #}
      <a data-testid="store-header-mobile-toggle"
         class="lg:hidden mburger mburger--collapse leading-none mp-header__burger"
         href="#mobile-menu" aria-label="Open menu">
        <i class="sicon-menu text-2xl"></i>
      </a>

      {# ---- Brand ---------------------------------------------------------
         Moved UP from the old second row. noon's logo sits in the accent bar
         beside the search, not on a separate white line below it. #}
      <a data-testid="store-header-logo" class="navbar-brand mp-header__logo" href="{{ store.url }}">
        <img fetchpriority="high" width="100%" height="100%" loading="eager"
             src="{{ store.logo|cdn(175) }}" alt="{{ store.name }} logo">
        {% if is_page('index') %}
          <h1 class="sr-only">{{ store.name }}</h1>
        {% else %}
          <h2 class="sr-only">{{ store.name }}</h2>
        {% endif %}
      </a>

      {# ---- Location / branch scope ---------------------------------------
         noon leads with "Deliver to Riyadh". Same idea: if the store has
         branches, the shopper's branch belongs beside the logo, not buried. #}
      {% if store.scope %}
        <button class="mp-header__scope"
                onclick="salla.event.dispatch('scopes::open', {'mode': 'default'})">
          <i class="sicon-location" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span class="mp-header__scope-name">{{ store.scope.name }}</span>
        </button>
      {% endif %}

      {# ---- Search - the widest element in the row ------------------------ #}
      <div class="header-search mp-header__search">
        <salla-search data-testid="store-header-search" inline oval height="40"></salla-search>
      </div>

      {# ---- Right-hand actions -------------------------------------------- #}
      <div class="mp-header__actions">

        {% if store.settings.is_multilingual or store.settings.currencies_enabled %}
          <div class="header-buttons mp-header__lang">
            <salla-localization-modal data-testid="store-header-localization" show-trigger></salla-localization-modal>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {# Desktop-only delivery tag; the mobile instance is the row above. #}
        <div class="hidden lg:block">
          <salla-bullet-delivery-tag></salla-bullet-delivery-tag>
        </div>

        <salla-user-menu data-testid="store-header-user-menu"
                         class="mp-header__user"
                         avatar-only show-header show-trigger></salla-user-menu>

        <salla-cart-summary data-testid="store-header-cart" class="mp-header__cart">
          <i slot="icon" class="header-btn__icon icon sicon-shopping-bag"></i>
        </salla-cart-summary>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# ==========================================================================
     ROW 2 - category rail
     --------------------------------------------------------------------------
     One fixed-height line that scrolls sideways instead of wrapping. A nav
     that wraps changes the header's height with the number of categories a
     merchant happens to have, and every sticky offset underneath it drifts.
     Fixed height is what keeps the rest of the page honest.
     ========================================================================== #}
  <div id="mainnav" class="main-nav-container mp-header__nav">
    <div class="container mp-header__nav-inner">
      <custom-main-menu></custom-main-menu>

      {# Contacts pushed to the end of the category line - noon runs its
         "Get free delivery" pill in the same position. #}
      <salla-contacts data-testid="store-header-contacts" class="mp-header__contacts" is-header></salla-contacts>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# Merchant-configured "important links" menu. Kept because removing it
     would silently drop a menu the merchant set up, but it is low priority,
     so it renders last and is hidden on small screens by CSS, not deleted. #}
  {% if important_links %}
    <div class="mp-header__utility">
      <div class="container">
        <salla-menu data-testid="store-header-topnav" source="footer" topnav></salla-menu>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</header>
